@node linear-phase-eq Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Linear-phase parametric EQ with FIR convolution for zero phase distortion.

@subsubheading What It Does

A parametric equalizer that uses FIR (Finite Impulse Response) filters instead of traditional IIR biquads. This eliminates phase distortion entirely — all frequencies are delayed by the same amount. The tradeoff is higher latency compared to a minimum-phase EQ.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Zero phase distortion}: All frequencies delayed equally
@item @strong{FIR convolution}: Uses frequency-domain convolution for efficient processing
@item @strong{Parametric bands}: Standard frequency, Q, and gain controls
@item @strong{High precision}: Ideal for mastering and critical listening
@end itemize


